WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.189 --> 00:00:01.650
(dramatic music)

00:00:01.650 --> 00:00:05.680
- [Narrator] Santander,
Colombia, rich with wildlife

00:00:06.670 --> 00:00:11.670
such as the majestic and
delicious big-ass ant.

00:00:11.771 --> 00:00:12.604
(tape screeches)

00:00:12.604 --> 00:00:15.000
I am so sorry for that
terrible impression.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:16.160
Let's go and eat some ants.

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:17.523
Roll the title.

00:00:24.040 --> 00:00:26.280
These are hormigas culonas

00:00:26.280 --> 00:00:28.650
otherwise known as big-ass ants.

00:00:28.650 --> 00:00:31.360
No, really that's the name.

00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:33.360
Here in San Gil, people love to snack

00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:36.100
on the little critters,
but to get them fresh

00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:37.210
they have to move quick,

00:00:37.210 --> 00:00:39.820
as they're only above
ground for one day a year.

00:00:39.820 --> 00:00:44.380
Yes, that's 24 hours only
to get your ants fresh.

00:00:44.380 --> 00:00:45.530
This is Adrian.

00:00:45.530 --> 00:00:47.873
He's an expert when it
come to hunting them.

00:01:39.954 --> 00:01:40.787
- [Narrator] Yeah, I'm like that

00:01:40.787 --> 00:01:42.010
with the Flamin' Hot Cheetos.

00:01:42.010 --> 00:01:44.280
Anyway, what if you're
looking for something

00:01:44.280 --> 00:01:46.050
a little more restaurant-friendly?

00:01:46.050 --> 00:01:47.543
What would you suggest, Elsa?

00:02:31.643 --> 00:02:35.388
- [Narrator] And now the most
important part, the taste.

00:02:35.388 --> 00:02:36.810
(moaning appreciatively) Pretty good.

00:02:36.810 --> 00:02:38.150
Tastes like chicken.

